msgstr "Inline limit"

msgid "Trimmed CSS is written into <head> up to this size; anything beyond is loaded as a separate cached file. 0 = always a file."
msgstr "Trimmed CSS is written into <head> up to this size; anything beyond is loaded as a separate cached file. 0 = always a file."

msgid "Always keep these classes"
msgstr "Always keep these classes"

msgid "One class or id per line, * as wildcard. If a style added later by JavaScript breaks, add its class here. is-*, has-*, wp-*, swiper-* are always kept."
msgstr "One class or id per line, * as wildcard. If a style added later by JavaScript breaks, add its class here. is-*, has-*, wp-*, swiper-* are always kept."

msgid "Remove unused CSS and inline it"
msgstr "Remove unused CSS and inline it"

msgid "Each page's class/id inventory is collected (HTML + the page's scripts); rules with no match on that page are dropped from the CSS file and the rest is written into <head>. The render-blocking CSS request goes away and LCP/FCP improve. Pages with the same inventory share one copy; copies are rebuilt when the file changes, and the full file is used if there are too many different pages."
msgstr "Each page's class/id inventory is collected (HTML + the page's scripts); rules with no match on that page are dropped from the CSS file and the rest is written into <head>. The render-blocking CSS request goes away and LCP/FCP improve. Pages with the same inventory share one copy; copies are rebuilt when the file changes, and the full file is used if there are too many different pages."

msgid "Minify CSS files"
msgstr "Minify CSS files"

msgid "For unminified (non-.min) local CSS files, an up-to-date .min sibling or a copy without comments and whitespace is used."
msgstr "For unminified (non-.min) local CSS files, an up-to-date .min sibling or a copy without comments and whitespace is used."

msgid "Minify JS files"
msgstr "Minify JS files"

msgid "For theme and plugin scripts, the .min sibling is used if it is newer than the source; otherwise a copy without comments and indentation is generated (line breaks are kept). Bundles that load chunks relative to their own location and scripts with translations are left alone."
msgstr "For theme and plugin scripts, the .min sibling is used if it is newer than the source; otherwise a copy without comments and indentation is generated (line breaks are kept). Bundles that load chunks relative to their own location and scripts with translations are left alone."

msgid "jQuery always stays blocking (older inline scripts on the page may call it directly). WordPress itself drops defer for scripts that have an inline script after them or that a blocking script depends on."
msgstr "jQuery always stays blocking (older inline scripts on the page may call it directly). WordPress itself drops defer for scripts that have an inline script after them or that a blocking script depends on."

msgid "Defer head scripts"
msgstr "Defer head scripts"

msgid "Scripts loaded in the page <head> that hold up rendering get defer (e.g. language suggestion, analytics scripts)."
msgstr "Scripts loaded in the page <head> that hold up rendering get defer (e.g. language suggestion, analytics scripts)."

